1
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:05,798
( snoring loudly )

2
00:00:08,509 --> 00:00:11,846
ARE YOU KIDDING ME?

3
00:00:13,722 --> 00:00:16,015
JOEY. JOEY.

4
00:00:16,057 --> 00:00:19,603
JOEY. JOEY, JOEY,
JOEY, JOEY, JOEY...

5
00:00:19,645 --> 00:00:22,982
JOEY... JOEY... JOEY.

6
00:00:23,022 --> 00:00:25,526
JOEY. JOEY!

7
00:00:27,235 --> 00:00:28,696
( whispers ):
ALL RIGHT!

8
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:36,036
( resumes snoring )

9
00:00:40,374 --> 00:00:43,126
OH, OH, DID-DID...
DID I WAKE YOU?

10
00:00:50,091 --> 00:00:55,055
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

11
00:00:55,096 --> 00:00:57,349
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

12
00:00:57,391 --> 00:00:59,601
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

13
00:00:59,643 --> 00:01:04,606
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

14
00:01:04,648 --> 00:01:07,026
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN YOUR DAY ♪

15
00:01:07,067 --> 00:01:10,153
♪ YOUR WEEK, YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

16
00:01:10,195 --> 00:01:13,699
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

17
00:01:13,741 --> 00:01:16,076
♪ WHEN THE RAIN
STARTS TO POUR ♪

18
00:01:16,117 --> 00:01:18,746
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

19
00:01:18,787 --> 00:01:20,873
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

20
00:01:20,915 --> 00:01:23,667
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

21
00:01:23,709 --> 00:01:29,631
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

22
00:01:34,261 --> 00:01:35,846
GUNTHER, COULD I GET

23
00:01:35,888 --> 00:01:38,849
ANOTHER CUP OF
COFFEE, PLEASE?

24
00:01:38,891 --> 00:01:42,644
SO, UH, WHAT DO
YOU DO WHEN YOU'RE
NOT WORKING HERE?

25
00:01:42,686 --> 00:01:44,605
YOU DON'T NEED
TO FILL THESE 
SILENCES.

26
00:01:44,646 --> 00:01:46,147
OH, OKAY, THANKS.

27
00:01:47,524 --> 00:01:48,943
CHANDLER,
THAT'S, LIKE

28
00:01:48,984 --> 00:01:50,819
YOUR FOURTH
CUP OF COFFEE.

29
00:01:50,861 --> 00:01:53,113
I AM DRINKING LOTS
BECAUSE I AM EXHAUSTED

30
00:01:53,154 --> 00:01:54,782
BECAUSE JOEY STARTED SNORING.

31
00:01:54,823 --> 00:01:57,116
HE'S IN A
DIFFERENT ROOM.

32
00:01:57,158 --> 00:01:58,577
HE'S REALLY THAT LOUD?

33
00:01:58,619 --> 00:02:00,203
OH, YOU SHOULD HEAR ME.

34
00:02:00,245 --> 00:02:01,830
IT'S NOTHING TO BE PROUD OF.

35
00:02:01,872 --> 00:02:03,665
YOU HAVE TO GO
TO A SLEEP CLINIC.

36
00:02:03,707 --> 00:02:06,167
I TOLD YOU
I'M NOT GOING
TO ANY CLINIC.

37
00:02:06,209 --> 00:02:07,920
YOU'RE THE ONE
WITH THE PROBLEM.

38
00:02:07,962 --> 00:02:09,379
YOU SHOULD GO

39
00:02:09,421 --> 00:02:12,173
TO A QUIT-BEING-A-BABY-
AND-LEAVE-ME-ALONE CLINIC.

40
00:02:12,215 --> 00:02:14,509
THEY DON'T
HAVE THOSE.

41
00:02:14,551 --> 00:02:15,719
YEAH, THEY DO.

42
00:02:15,761 --> 00:02:18,013
QUIT BEING A BABY
AND LEAVE ME ALONE.

43
00:02:18,055 --> 00:02:19,681
THERE, YOU JUST HAD

44
00:02:19,723 --> 00:02:21,349
YOUR FIRST CLASS.

45
00:02:21,391 --> 00:02:23,018
I USED TO GO OUT
WITH THIS GUY

46
00:02:23,060 --> 00:02:24,686
THAT WAS A REALLY
LIGHT SLEEPER

47
00:02:24,728 --> 00:02:26,396
AND WHENEVER I'D
START TO SNORE

48
00:02:26,438 --> 00:02:27,815
HE'D JUST ROLL
ME OVER...

49
00:02:27,856 --> 00:02:29,691
OH, YEAH...

50
00:02:31,443 --> 00:02:32,820
HE WOULD JUST
ROLL ME OVER

51
00:02:32,861 --> 00:02:34,195
AND I WOULD
STOP SNORING.

52
00:02:34,237 --> 00:02:37,156
NEXT TIME YOU SNORE,
I'M ROLLING YOU OVER.

53
00:02:37,198 --> 00:02:38,700
I GOT TO DO
WHAT I GOT TO DO.

54
00:02:38,742 --> 00:02:40,535
YOU GOT TO DO
WHAT YOU GOT TO DO.

55
00:02:40,577 --> 00:02:41,662
JUST DO IT.

56
00:02:41,703 --> 00:02:42,663
HEY, GUYS.

57
00:02:42,704 --> 00:02:44,081
HEY.
HEY.

58
00:02:44,123 --> 00:02:47,793
( humming
"The Wedding March" )

59
00:02:47,835 --> 00:02:49,503
OH, THE OLYMPICS.

60
00:02:51,588 --> 00:02:53,256
HAVE YOU GUYS
PICKED A DATE?

61
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:54,967
HUH? OH, NO, NOT YET.

62
00:02:55,009 --> 00:02:57,552
I STILL CANNOT BELIEVE
YOU'RE ENGAGED.

63
00:02:57,594 --> 00:02:59,138
JUST 'CAUSE

64
00:02:59,178 --> 00:03:02,349
IT'S HAPPENING SO FAST,
NOT 'CAUSE YOU'RE SUCH A LOSER.

65
00:03:02,390 --> 00:03:06,436
THANKS. UH, HAS
ANYONE SEEN RACH?

66
00:03:06,478 --> 00:03:08,605
OH, SHE'S UPSTAIRS
NOT DOING THE DISHES.

67
00:03:08,647 --> 00:03:09,690
AND I'LL TELL
YOU SOMETHING.

68
00:03:09,731 --> 00:03:10,983
YOU KNOW, I'M NOT
DOING THEM THIS TIME.

69
00:03:11,025 --> 00:03:12,567
I DON'T CARE IF THOSE
DISHES JUST SIT IN THE SINK

70
00:03:12,609 --> 00:03:14,153
UNTIL THEY'RE ALL
COVERED WITH...

71
00:03:14,193 --> 00:03:17,698
I'LL DO THEM
WHEN I GET HOME.

72
00:03:17,739 --> 00:03:19,074
YEAH. OH, HEY, LISTEN

73
00:03:19,116 --> 00:03:21,409
EMILY FOUND THIS WEDDING DRESS
IN LONDON...

74
00:03:21,451 --> 00:03:22,494
ALREADY?

75
00:03:22,536 --> 00:03:23,954
YEAH, BUT IT
DIDN'T FIT.

76
00:03:23,996 --> 00:03:26,414
LUCKILY, A STORE
HERE HAS ONE LEFT
IN HER SIZE

77
00:03:26,456 --> 00:03:29,292
BUT I'M THE GROOM--
I'M NOT SUPPOSED TO
SEE THE DRESS...

78
00:03:29,334 --> 00:03:30,585
I'LL PICK
IT UP FOR YOU.

79
00:03:30,627 --> 00:03:32,546
WHOA, SHE'S GOT YOU
RUNNING ERRANDS

80
00:03:32,587 --> 00:03:35,007
YOU KNOW,
PICKING UP WEDDING DRESSES...

81
00:03:35,049 --> 00:03:36,050
WAH-PAH!

82
00:03:39,178 --> 00:03:41,346
WHAT'S "WAH-PAH"?

83
00:03:41,388 --> 00:03:43,431
YOU KNOW-- WHIPPED.

84
00:03:43,473 --> 00:03:44,474
WAH-PAH!

85
00:03:47,519 --> 00:03:49,228
THAT'S NOT "WHIPPED."

86
00:03:49,270 --> 00:03:50,271
"WHIPPED" IS...

87
00:03:50,313 --> 00:03:51,398
WA-TSSH!

88
00:03:53,650 --> 00:03:55,402
THAT'S WHAT I DID.

89
00:03:55,443 --> 00:03:56,611
WAH-PAH!

90
00:03:57,988 --> 00:04:00,574
YOU CAN'T DO ANYTHING!

91
00:04:09,583 --> 00:04:12,127
( footsteps approaching )

92
00:04:15,047 --> 00:04:16,131
HEY, MON...

93
00:04:16,173 --> 00:04:17,925
I WAS JUST DOING
THESE DISHES...

94
00:04:17,966 --> 00:04:18,926
HEY.
OH.

95
00:04:18,967 --> 00:04:20,928
OH. IT'S YOU. HI.

96
00:04:20,969 --> 00:04:22,763
HEY, DO YOU HAVE A MINUTE?

97
00:04:22,804 --> 00:04:25,974
YEAH, YEAH. I WAS JUST GOING
TO TAKE A BREAK ANYWAY SO...

98
00:04:26,016 --> 00:04:27,350
WHEW!

99
00:04:27,392 --> 00:04:31,021
SO, LISTEN, UH...
I KNOW YOU AND I

100
00:04:31,063 --> 00:04:32,981
HAVEN'T REALLY HAD
A CHANCE TO TALK

101
00:04:33,023 --> 00:04:36,110
SINCE, UH... EMILY AND I
DECIDED TO GET MARRIED

102
00:04:36,151 --> 00:04:38,195
AND I WAS JUST
WONDERING HOW YOU WERE.

103
00:04:38,237 --> 00:04:39,238
( clears throat )

104
00:04:39,279 --> 00:04:40,655
OH.

105
00:04:40,697 --> 00:04:42,824
I MEAN, I KNOW
IF YOU WERE GETTING MARRIED

106
00:04:42,866 --> 00:04:45,284
UH, I MEAN,
I WOULD FEEL, UM, KIND OF...

107
00:04:47,287 --> 00:04:48,830
YOU KNOW? UH...

108
00:04:48,872 --> 00:04:50,331
YEAH, YEAH. IT DEF...

109
00:04:50,373 --> 00:04:52,459
IT DEFINITELY, UH,
TOOK ME BY SURPRISE

110
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:55,170
BUT, YOU KNOW, UH...
I'M OKAY.

111
00:04:55,212 --> 00:04:56,171
YEAH?

112
00:04:56,213 --> 00:04:57,798
YEAH, YOU KNOW.
I'M OKAY.

113
00:04:57,839 --> 00:04:59,674
ALL RIGHT.
I JUST WANTED TO CHECK.

114
00:04:59,716 --> 00:05:01,384
OH, THAT'S SWEET. THANK YOU.

115
00:05:01,426 --> 00:05:03,511
( both chuckle )

116
00:05:03,553 --> 00:05:04,679
YOU'RE GREAT.

117
00:05:04,721 --> 00:05:06,765
AND I-I KNOW SOMEDAY
THIS WILL HAPPEN

118
00:05:06,807 --> 00:05:08,600
FOR YOU, TOO, YOU KNOW?

119
00:05:10,227 --> 00:05:12,353
YOU JUST HANG IN THERE.

120
00:05:12,395 --> 00:05:13,647
UH...

121
00:05:13,688 --> 00:05:14,648
( chuckles )

122
00:05:14,689 --> 00:05:16,566
"HANG IN THERE"?

123
00:05:16,608 --> 00:05:18,526
OH, NO, I-I DIDN'T MEAN, UH...

124
00:05:18,568 --> 00:05:20,862
I MEAN, MAYBE YOU HAVE
NOT HEARD OF A LITTLE

125
00:05:20,904 --> 00:05:23,115
SERIOUS RELATIONSHIP
CALLED "ME AND JOSHUA"?

126
00:05:23,157 --> 00:05:25,784
OH. UH,
I THOUGHT YOU GUYS

127
00:05:25,826 --> 00:05:27,869
HAD JUST BEEN
ON, LIKE, FOUR DATES.

128
00:05:27,911 --> 00:05:29,871
I DIDN'T REALIZE THAT HAD...

129
00:05:29,913 --> 00:05:31,248
BECOME ANYTHING.

130
00:05:31,290 --> 00:05:33,875
OH, YEAH. NO, OH, NO;
OH, NO, THAT HAS BECOME.

131
00:05:33,917 --> 00:05:35,294
OH.
IT HAS. YEAH.

132
00:05:35,335 --> 00:05:37,545
OH, NO, THOSE WERE
FOUR GREAT DATES.

133
00:05:37,587 --> 00:05:39,089
OH. YEAH?

134
00:05:39,131 --> 00:05:41,382
OH, YEAH. OH, I MEAN,
AND THE CONNECTION?

135
00:05:41,424 --> 00:05:43,051
I MEAN, YOU KNOW...

136
00:05:43,093 --> 00:05:46,721
EMOTIONALLY,
MENTALLY, YOU KNOW?

137
00:05:46,763 --> 00:05:48,598
PHYSICALLY.

138
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:50,934
WOW, THAT'S-THAT'S-THAT'S
INCREDIBLE.

139
00:05:50,976 --> 00:05:52,477
I KNOW. ISN'T IT?

140
00:05:52,519 --> 00:05:54,562
IT'S LIKE I'M RIGHT
THERE WITH JOSHUA;

141
00:05:54,604 --> 00:05:56,231
YOU ARE RIGHT
THERE WITH EMILY;

142
00:05:56,273 --> 00:05:58,483
AND IT'S, YOU KNOW,
IT'S KIND OF LIKE...

143
00:05:58,525 --> 00:05:59,651
IT'S A TIE.

144
00:05:59,693 --> 00:06:01,653
( chuckles )

145
00:06:01,695 --> 00:06:03,197
YEAH, WELL, I
GOT TO GET...

146
00:06:03,238 --> 00:06:05,740
I GOT TO GET BACK
TO MY DISHES.

147
00:06:05,782 --> 00:06:07,242
I GOT TO GET TO WORK.

148
00:06:07,284 --> 00:06:08,576
OH, YEAH. OKAY.

149
00:06:08,618 --> 00:06:12,122
( clearing throat )

150
00:06:12,164 --> 00:06:15,334
HEY, YOU KNOW WHAT WOULD
MAKE ME REALLY HAPPY?

151
00:06:15,374 --> 00:06:17,252
OH, YOU KNOW, WHAT'S THAT?

152
00:06:17,294 --> 00:06:18,753
IF, LIKE, THE FOUR OF US

153
00:06:18,795 --> 00:06:21,215
COULD ALL, YOU KNOW,
HANG OUT TOGETHER.

154
00:06:21,256 --> 00:06:23,758
IN FACT, EMILY'S COMING
INTO TOWN THIS WEEKEND.

155
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:26,678
WHAT DO YOU SAY WE ALL HAVE
DINNER, SAY, SUNDAY NIGHT?

156
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:28,555
THAT WOULD BE GREAT!

157
00:06:28,596 --> 00:06:29,848
YEAH?

158
00:06:29,890 --> 00:06:31,725
ALL RIGHT, ALL RIGHT.
IT'S A DATE.

159
00:06:31,766 --> 00:06:32,726
YEAH.

160
00:06:32,767 --> 00:06:34,144
"HANG IN THERE."

161
00:06:34,186 --> 00:06:36,021
YOU HANG IN THERE.

162
00:06:36,063 --> 00:06:37,772
( gasps )

163
00:06:37,814 --> 00:06:38,815
YOU SAY SOMETHING?

164
00:06:38,857 --> 00:06:40,234
NO, I WAS JUST SINGING.

165
00:06:41,818 --> 00:06:44,321
♪ LA-LA-LA,
LA-LA-LA-LA... ♪

166
00:06:46,823 --> 00:06:48,742
OH, MY GOD.

167
00:06:48,783 --> 00:06:51,619
( both gasp )

168
00:06:51,661 --> 00:06:53,330
OH, LOOK AT THIS ONE.

169
00:06:53,372 --> 00:06:54,331
WOW.

170
00:06:54,373 --> 00:06:55,957
OH, IT'S SO BEAUTIFUL.

171
00:06:55,999 --> 00:06:58,043
YEAH, OOH...

172
00:06:58,085 --> 00:07:00,461
WELL, YOU KNOW,
ABOUT HALF OF THESE

173
00:07:00,503 --> 00:07:02,589
ARE GOING TO END UP
GETTING DIVORCED.

174
00:07:02,630 --> 00:07:04,216
MAY I HELP YOU,
LADIES?

175
00:07:04,258 --> 00:07:05,967
YES, I'M HERE TO
PICK UP A DRESS

176
00:07:06,009 --> 00:07:07,135
THAT YOU
HAVE ON HOLD.

177
00:07:07,177 --> 00:07:08,469
WHAT'S THE NAME, PLEASE?

178
00:07:08,511 --> 00:07:09,512
EMILY WALTHAM.

179
00:07:09,554 --> 00:07:11,973
OH, YES,
I HAVE IT RIGHT HERE.

180
00:07:14,309 --> 00:07:15,352
( Monica gasps )

181
00:07:15,394 --> 00:07:16,937
OH, MY...

182
00:07:16,978 --> 00:07:19,522
WOULD YOU LIKE
TO TRY IT ON, MISS WALTHAM?

183
00:07:19,564 --> 00:07:21,358
( both giggle )

184
00:07:24,527 --> 00:07:26,487
OKAY.

185
00:07:32,452 --> 00:07:36,290
YOU'RE THE MOST BEAUTIFUL BRIDE
I'VE EVER SEEN.

186
00:07:36,331 --> 00:07:38,166
I AM, AREN'T I?

187
00:07:38,208 --> 00:07:39,918
YEAH.

188
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:40,919
( sighs )

189
00:07:40,961 --> 00:07:42,296
MISS WALTHAM.

190
00:07:42,337 --> 00:07:43,297
YES?

191
00:07:43,338 --> 00:07:44,547
WE'RE CLOSING.

192
00:07:47,050 --> 00:07:48,885
ALL RIGHT.

193
00:07:48,927 --> 00:07:50,929
AND COULD I GET
MY RING BACK?

194
00:07:55,058 --> 00:07:59,229
( snoring )

195
00:08:01,940 --> 00:08:03,650
ALL RIGHT, BUDDY.

196
00:08:03,691 --> 00:08:05,402
TIME TO ROLL OVER.

197
00:08:08,363 --> 00:08:11,283
NO, NO!
NO, NO, NO, NO, NO!

198
00:08:11,325 --> 00:08:13,576
YOU ARE GOING TO A CLINIC.

199
00:08:13,618 --> 00:08:16,871
YOU'RE GOING TO A CLINIC...

200
00:08:16,913 --> 00:08:18,415
AND A PAJAMA STORE.

201
00:08:23,962 --> 00:08:25,713
DOES SHE USE THE CUPS?

202
00:08:25,755 --> 00:08:27,674
YES, I BELIEVE SHE DOES.

203
00:08:29,676 --> 00:08:31,345
DOES SHE USE THE PLATES?

204
00:08:31,386 --> 00:08:33,512
YES, I BELIEVE SHE DOES.

205
00:08:39,769 --> 00:08:40,812
( chuckles )

206
00:08:42,689 --> 00:08:43,690
THANK YOU.

207
00:08:45,608 --> 00:08:49,070
AW... THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

208
00:08:49,112 --> 00:08:51,614
OH, WELL, THANK YOU FOR COMING.

209
00:08:52,991 --> 00:08:55,243
( knock at door )

210
00:08:55,285 --> 00:08:56,619
UH, JUST A SECOND!

211
00:08:56,661 --> 00:08:58,413
Phoebe:
NO, NO, LET ME IN.

212
00:08:58,455 --> 00:08:59,414
PHOEBE?

213
00:08:59,456 --> 00:09:00,499
YEAH.

214
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:02,250
CAN YOU HOLD ON
JUST ONE MINUTE?

215
00:09:02,292 --> 00:09:05,420
NO, YOU HAVE TO LET
ME IN RIGHT NOW!

216
00:09:05,462 --> 00:09:06,838
ARE YOU ALONE?

217
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:08,465
YES.

218
00:09:08,507 --> 00:09:09,508
ALL RIGHT.

219
00:09:11,843 --> 00:09:13,720
( giggles )

220
00:09:13,761 --> 00:09:14,804
( both scream )

221
00:09:17,932 --> 00:09:19,393
THIS SUCKS.

222
00:09:19,434 --> 00:09:21,728
I DIDN'T KNOW
I HAD TO STAY UP ALL NIGHT

223
00:09:21,769 --> 00:09:24,105
BEFORE I GO
TO THIS STUPID SLEEP CLINIC.

224
00:09:24,147 --> 00:09:25,564
I'M SO TIRED.

225
00:09:25,606 --> 00:09:28,151
IT'S 6:00.

226
00:09:29,486 --> 00:09:30,778
HI.

227
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:32,197
HEY, I HEAR
YOU AND JOSHUA

228
00:09:32,239 --> 00:09:34,574
ARE GOING OUT TO DINNER
WITH ROSS AND EMILY.

229
00:09:34,615 --> 00:09:36,910
I THINK THAT'S--
I THINK THAT'S REALLY COOL.

230
00:09:36,951 --> 00:09:39,371
YEAH, RACHEL,
I THINK YOU'RE HANDLING THAT

231
00:09:39,413 --> 00:09:40,455
REALLY WELL.

232
00:09:40,497 --> 00:09:42,623
WHAT DO YOU MEAN,
"HANDLING" IT?

233
00:09:42,665 --> 00:09:44,209
THERE'S NOTHING
TO HANDLE.

234
00:09:44,251 --> 00:09:46,753
YOU KNOW, MAYBE I WOULD HAVE
A PROBLEM WITH THIS

235
00:09:46,794 --> 00:09:48,505
IF IT WASN'T
FOR ME AND JOSHUA.

236
00:09:48,547 --> 00:09:51,174
YOU KNOW, THEY'RE NOT GOING
TO GET MARRIED ANYWAY.

237
00:09:51,216 --> 00:09:52,509
WHAT?

238
00:09:52,551 --> 00:09:54,969
COME ON. THEY RUSHED
INTO THIS THING SO FAST

239
00:09:55,011 --> 00:09:56,555
IT'S RIDICULOUS.

240
00:09:56,596 --> 00:09:59,516
THEY'RE GOING TO BE ENGAGED
FOR, LIKE, WHAT, A YEAR?

241
00:09:59,558 --> 00:10:02,018
ONE OF THEM WILL REALIZE
WHAT THEY'VE DONE

242
00:10:02,060 --> 00:10:04,020
AND THEY'LL CALL
THE WHOLE THING OFF.

243
00:10:04,062 --> 00:10:06,231
YOU'RE GOING TO BE
DANCING AT MY WEDDING

244
00:10:06,273 --> 00:10:07,899
BEFORE YOU'RE DANCING
AT THEIRS.

245
00:10:07,941 --> 00:10:09,943
YEAH, WELL, I DON'T
DANCE AT WEDDINGS.

246
00:10:09,984 --> 00:10:11,486
WHY NOT?

247
00:10:11,528 --> 00:10:14,155
BECAUSE WEDDINGS ARE
A GREAT PLACE TO MEET WOMEN

248
00:10:14,197 --> 00:10:16,741
AND WHEN I DANCE,
I LOOK LIKE THIS:

249
00:10:26,042 --> 00:10:27,252
HEY, MAN.

250
00:10:27,294 --> 00:10:28,462
HEY.

251
00:10:30,213 --> 00:10:32,673
SO, WHAT'RE YOU GUYS DOING
FOUR WEEKS FROM TODAY?

252
00:10:32,715 --> 00:10:33,300
NOTHING.

253
00:10:33,341 --> 00:10:34,175
NOTHING.

254
00:10:34,217 --> 00:10:35,427
I AM...

255
00:10:37,429 --> 00:10:39,013
FREE.

256
00:10:39,055 --> 00:10:42,892
GREAT, BECAUSE EMILY AND I
ARE GETTING MARRIED IN A MONTH.

257
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:45,145
WHAT?
WHAT?

258
00:10:45,186 --> 00:10:46,146
YEP.

259
00:10:46,187 --> 00:10:47,481
IN A MONTH?
YEAH.

260
00:10:47,522 --> 00:10:48,856
YOU MEAN, 30 DAYS?

261
00:10:48,898 --> 00:10:49,941
YEAH.

262
00:10:49,983 --> 00:10:51,109
FROM NOW.

263
00:10:51,151 --> 00:10:52,110
YEAH.

264
00:10:52,152 --> 00:10:53,820
OH, THAT'S GREAT!

265
00:10:53,861 --> 00:10:55,071
EMILY ALWAYS WANTED

266
00:10:55,113 --> 00:10:57,157
TO GET MARRIED
IN THIS BEAUTIFUL PLACE

267
00:10:57,198 --> 00:10:58,699
THAT HER PARENTS GOT MARRIED

268
00:10:58,741 --> 00:11:00,743
BUT IT'S GOING
TO BE TORN DOWN, SO...

269
00:11:00,785 --> 00:11:02,370
I MEAN, I-I KNOW IT'S CRAZY

270
00:11:02,412 --> 00:11:04,998
BUT EVERYTHING UP TILL NOW
HAS BEEN SO CRAZY

271
00:11:05,039 --> 00:11:07,750
AND, I DON'T KNOW--
IT JUST FEELS RIGHT, YOU KNOW?

272
00:11:07,792 --> 00:11:09,377
HEY...

273
00:11:09,419 --> 00:11:11,879
THAT'S THE DAY
AFTER I START MENSTRUATING.

274
00:11:21,556 --> 00:11:23,391
THIS ISN'T MINE.

275
00:11:32,817 --> 00:11:33,985
( clears throat )

276
00:11:34,027 --> 00:11:34,986
HEY, RACHEL.

277
00:11:35,028 --> 00:11:36,530
HI.

278
00:11:36,571 --> 00:11:38,156
WHAT'S UP?

279
00:11:38,198 --> 00:11:41,326
YOUR VOICE SOUNDED ALL
SQUEAKY ON THE PHONE.

280
00:11:41,368 --> 00:11:42,369
OH... NOTHING.

281
00:11:42,410 --> 00:11:44,245
I JUST WANTED TO SEE YOU.

282
00:11:44,287 --> 00:11:45,664
SEE YOU AND HUG YOU.

283
00:11:45,704 --> 00:11:47,666
S-SEE YOU...

284
00:11:47,706 --> 00:11:48,707
GREAT.

285
00:11:48,749 --> 00:11:50,709
YEAH, SO...

286
00:11:50,751 --> 00:11:52,086
SIT.

287
00:11:53,630 --> 00:11:54,589
( clears throat )

288
00:11:54,631 --> 00:11:55,590
( sighs )

289
00:11:55,632 --> 00:11:57,133
YOU OKAY?

290
00:11:57,175 --> 00:11:59,386
I'M MORE THAN OKAY.

291
00:11:59,427 --> 00:12:02,681
I AM REALLY, REALLY HAPPY.

292
00:12:05,016 --> 00:12:06,393
WANT TO KNOW WHY?

293
00:12:06,434 --> 00:12:08,061
DO I?

294
00:12:08,102 --> 00:12:11,606
'CAUSE I AM REALLY HAPPY
ABOUT US.

295
00:12:11,648 --> 00:12:12,982
I THINK WE ARE...

296
00:12:13,024 --> 00:12:14,984
I THINK WE ARE
SO ON THE RIGHT TRACK.

297
00:12:15,026 --> 00:12:16,653
YOU KNOW? I MEAN

298
00:12:16,695 --> 00:12:18,029
I THINK WE ARE WORKING.

299
00:12:18,071 --> 00:12:19,447
I THINK WE ARE CLICKING.

300
00:12:19,489 --> 00:12:20,574
YOU KNOW?

301
00:12:20,615 --> 00:12:21,740
YEAH, SURE, SURE.

302
00:12:21,782 --> 00:12:23,577
YEAH, WE'RE-WE'RE-
WE'RE CLICKING.

303
00:12:23,618 --> 00:12:25,078
YEAH, YEAH, YOU KNOW

304
00:12:25,119 --> 00:12:27,746
IF-IF THERE WAS JUST, LIKE,
ONE LITTLE AREA WHERE...

305
00:12:27,788 --> 00:12:30,083
THAT I THINK
WE-WE WOULD NEED TO WORK ON...

306
00:12:30,124 --> 00:12:31,334
I-I WOULD THINK IT WAS

307
00:12:31,376 --> 00:12:33,127
THAT WE'RE
JUST NOT CRAZY ENOUGH.

308
00:12:33,169 --> 00:12:37,882
I-I GOT TO SAY I'M NOT
TOO SURE I AGREE WITH THAT.

309
00:12:37,924 --> 00:12:41,010
WELL, YEAH, RIGHT,
YOU KNOW, YEAH, YOU'RE RIGHT.

310
00:12:41,052 --> 00:12:44,097
I MEAN, WE... YOU KNOW,
WE HAVE OUR FUN, YEAH...

311
00:12:44,138 --> 00:12:45,682
BUT, IT'S... WE'RE JU...

312
00:12:45,724 --> 00:12:48,685
I MEAN, I MEAN, I MEAN, LIKE,
CRAZY, YOU KNOW?

313
00:12:48,727 --> 00:12:51,062
OKAY, ALL RIGHT.

314
00:12:51,104 --> 00:12:54,399
THIS IS GOING TO...
THIS IS GOING TO SOUND, YOU KNOW

315
00:12:54,441 --> 00:12:57,527
A LITTLE, UM... HASTY,
BUT, UH, JUST GO WITH ME.

316
00:12:57,569 --> 00:12:59,529
( clears throat )

317
00:12:59,571 --> 00:13:01,531
( sighs )

318
00:13:01,573 --> 00:13:03,991
WHAT IF WE GOT MARRIED?

319
00:13:07,579 --> 00:13:08,622
WHAT?

320
00:13:08,663 --> 00:13:10,290
OH, I KNOW, I KNOW.
IT'S SO...

321
00:13:10,331 --> 00:13:11,583
IT'S SO TOTALLY, LIKE

322
00:13:11,625 --> 00:13:13,167
WHOA, CAN WE DO THIS?

323
00:13:13,209 --> 00:13:16,421
YOU KNOW, I MEAN...
BUT I MEAN, IT JUST FEELS RIGHT.

324
00:13:16,463 --> 00:13:18,005
DON'T YOU THINK? IT DOES.

325
00:13:18,047 --> 00:13:20,550
I MEAN, IT JUST
FEELS RIGHT, DON'T...

326
00:13:20,592 --> 00:13:22,552
( whimpering )

327
00:13:22,594 --> 00:13:23,553
( sighs )

328
00:13:23,595 --> 00:13:25,555
WOW, UH...

329
00:13:25,597 --> 00:13:29,058
RACHEL, UM, YOU'RE...

330
00:13:29,100 --> 00:13:32,771
A REAL... SPECIAL LADY...

331
00:13:32,811 --> 00:13:35,356
BUT...

332
00:13:35,398 --> 00:13:37,609
MY DIVORCE
ISN'T FINAL YET

333
00:13:37,651 --> 00:13:40,737
AN-AN-AND WE'VE
BEEN ON FOUR DATES.

334
00:13:40,779 --> 00:13:41,904
SO...

335
00:13:41,946 --> 00:13:43,864
I'M THINKING...

336
00:13:43,906 --> 00:13:45,866
NO...

337
00:13:45,908 --> 00:13:47,535
BUT...

338
00:13:47,577 --> 00:13:48,703
THANKS.

339
00:13:50,955 --> 00:13:52,791
YOU IDIOT!

340
00:13:58,171 --> 00:13:59,255
YOUR NAME, PLEASE?

341
00:13:59,297 --> 00:14:00,674
JOEY TRIBBIANI.

342
00:14:00,715 --> 00:14:03,384
MM-HMM. DID YOU STAY UP
ALL NIGHT IN PREPARATION

343
00:14:03,426 --> 00:14:05,345
FOR YOUR
SLEEP STUDY?

344
00:14:05,386 --> 00:14:06,513
UH, SIR?

345
00:14:06,554 --> 00:14:09,390
( snoring )

346
00:14:09,432 --> 00:14:11,100
YES, HE DID.

347
00:14:11,142 --> 00:14:13,436
ALL RIGHT,
WE'LL CALL YOU
IN A FEW MINUTES.

348
00:14:13,478 --> 00:14:14,771
OKAY.

349
00:14:16,397 --> 00:14:17,440
WHOO.

350
00:14:17,482 --> 00:14:18,857
CHECK OUT THAT GIRL.

351
00:14:18,899 --> 00:14:20,318
SHE'S REALLY HOT.

352
00:14:22,278 --> 00:14:24,572
YEAH, SHE IS.

353
00:14:24,614 --> 00:14:25,948
WOW.

354
00:14:28,117 --> 00:14:29,868
HOW YOU DOING?

355
00:14:32,955 --> 00:14:34,081
WHAT?!

356
00:14:34,123 --> 00:14:36,751
YOU'RE COMING ON
TO THE ENTIRE ROOM.

357
00:14:42,799 --> 00:14:43,758
I'M CHANDLER.

358
00:14:43,800 --> 00:14:45,343
MARJORIE. HI.

359
00:14:45,385 --> 00:14:47,387
DO YOU MIND IF I SIT?
NO. PLEASE.

360
00:14:47,428 --> 00:14:49,096
SO, UH, WHAT
ARE YOU IN FOR?

361
00:14:49,138 --> 00:14:50,765
I-I TALK IN MY SLEEP.

362
00:14:50,807 --> 00:14:53,059
WHAT A COINCIDENCE;
I LISTEN IN MY SLEEP.

363
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:54,310
( laughing )

364
00:14:54,352 --> 00:14:57,355
SO WHY DON'T YOU
GIVE ME YOUR NUMBER?

365
00:15:00,692 --> 00:15:01,860
READY?
YEAH.

366
00:15:01,901 --> 00:15:03,027
OKAY.

367
00:15:05,405 --> 00:15:06,698
I GOT IT! MINE!

368
00:15:06,740 --> 00:15:08,533
( screams )

369
00:15:10,535 --> 00:15:11,619
CONGRATULATIONS!

370
00:15:11,661 --> 00:15:12,704
( laughing )

371
00:15:12,746 --> 00:15:13,872
OKAY...

372
00:15:13,913 --> 00:15:15,164
MY TURN! MY TURN!

373
00:15:15,206 --> 00:15:16,207
OKAY.

374
00:15:17,250 --> 00:15:18,251
OKAY, READY?

375
00:15:21,254 --> 00:15:22,338
YEAH.

376
00:15:22,380 --> 00:15:23,214
OKAY.

377
00:15:27,926 --> 00:15:30,221
THAT WAS A TERRIBLE THROW!

378
00:15:30,263 --> 00:15:33,099
WELL, I'M NOT GOING TO THROW IT
RIGHT TO YOU.

379
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:34,434
THAT'S NOT REAL.

380
00:15:34,475 --> 00:15:35,810
LOOK AT ME.

381
00:15:35,852 --> 00:15:37,854
MY BIG CONCERN IS WHAT'S REAL?

382
00:15:40,106 --> 00:15:42,024
OH, MY GOD.

383
00:15:42,066 --> 00:15:44,985
WE'RE REALLY SAD, AREN'T WE?

384
00:15:48,281 --> 00:15:49,908
YEAH, I THINK WE ARE.

385
00:15:49,949 --> 00:15:53,327
THIS ISN'T EVEN MY DRESS.

386
00:15:53,369 --> 00:15:56,038
YEAH, WELL, AT LEAST
YOU DIDN'T RENT YOURS

387
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:58,750
FROM A STORE CALLED
"IT'S NOT TOO LATE."

388
00:16:04,004 --> 00:16:05,882
I'M CHANGING OUT OF THIS.

389
00:16:05,924 --> 00:16:07,425
ME, TOO.

390
00:16:07,467 --> 00:16:09,968
IN, LIKE, A HALF AN HOUR?

391
00:16:10,010 --> 00:16:11,178
ME, TOO.

392
00:16:11,220 --> 00:16:12,513
OKAY. ALL RIGHT, NOW

393
00:16:12,555 --> 00:16:14,140
THROW IT STRAIGHT THIS TIME.

394
00:16:14,181 --> 00:16:15,892
OKAY.
OKAY.

395
00:16:15,934 --> 00:16:17,685
I'M GETTING MARRIED NEXT!

396
00:16:17,727 --> 00:16:18,937
YAY!

397
00:16:23,190 --> 00:16:27,111
I HATE MY REGULAR
CLOTHES NOW, YOU KNOW?

398
00:16:27,153 --> 00:16:29,196
IT'S LIKE I LOOK
DOWN AND-AND I KNOW

399
00:16:29,238 --> 00:16:31,741
THIS ISN'T GOING TO BE
THE MOST SPECIAL DAY

400
00:16:31,783 --> 00:16:33,075
OF MY LIFE.

401
00:16:33,117 --> 00:16:35,578
YEAH, I MEAN,
IT WAS KIND OF FUN FOR A WHILE

402
00:16:35,620 --> 00:16:38,247
BUT DIDN'T YOU START FEELING
KIND OF SILLY?

403
00:16:38,289 --> 00:16:39,248
I GUESS.

404
00:16:39,290 --> 00:16:40,583
YEAH.

405
00:16:40,625 --> 00:16:44,504
OH, MY GOD!

406
00:16:44,545 --> 00:16:45,588
OH!

407
00:16:45,630 --> 00:16:48,257
YOU'RE SUCH A CHEATER!

408
00:16:48,299 --> 00:16:49,509
HELLO, LITTLE ONES.

409
00:16:49,550 --> 00:16:50,593
HEY...
HEY...

410
00:16:50,635 --> 00:16:52,470
SO IS JOEY GOING
TO STOP SNORING?

411
00:16:52,512 --> 00:16:55,556
YEP, AND A BEAUTIFUL WOMAN
AGREED TO GO OUT WITH ME.

412
00:16:56,557 --> 00:16:58,267
JOEY WANTED TO ASK HER OUT

413
00:16:58,309 --> 00:17:00,478
BUT, UH, YOU KNOW,
SHE PICKED ME.

414
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:02,271
OH, HOW'D THAT HAPPEN?

415
00:17:03,731 --> 00:17:05,525
BECAUSE I'M COOLER.

416
00:17:05,566 --> 00:17:07,861
NO, SERIOUSLY.

417
00:17:09,362 --> 00:17:12,281
WELL, SHE'S, YOU KNOW,
SHE'S THE KIND OF GIRL...

418
00:17:12,323 --> 00:17:13,700
JOEY WAS UNCONSCIOUS.

419
00:17:16,410 --> 00:17:19,121
( mumbling ):
HEY, YOU GUYS,
WHAT'S HAPPENING?

420
00:17:19,163 --> 00:17:21,123
OH, MY GOD.

421
00:17:21,165 --> 00:17:22,458
WHAT IS THAT?

422
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:25,336
OH... THEY GAVE IT TO ME
AT THE SLEEP CLINIC

423
00:17:25,378 --> 00:17:28,047
AND IT'S GOING TO HELP ME
NOT TO SNORE.

424
00:17:28,088 --> 00:17:31,050
WELL, ARE YOU ASLEEP
RIGHT NOW, JOE?

425
00:17:31,091 --> 00:17:34,554
'CAUSE I DON'T THINK YOU HAVE
TO WEAR IT UNLESS YOU ARE.

426
00:17:34,595 --> 00:17:37,264
I KNOW I DON'T HAVE TO.

427
00:17:37,306 --> 00:17:39,099
IT TASTES GOOD.

428
00:17:41,143 --> 00:17:43,062
PLUS, YOU LOOK COOL.

429
00:17:48,860 --> 00:17:51,404
WELL, I JUST CALLED JOSHUA.

430
00:17:51,445 --> 00:17:52,572
OH, HOW'D IT GO?

431
00:17:52,613 --> 00:17:54,281
WELL, I DID MY BEST
TO CONVINCE HIM

432
00:17:54,323 --> 00:17:55,742
THAT I'M NOT SOME CRAZY GIRL

433
00:17:55,783 --> 00:17:57,827
WHO IS DYING TO GET MARRIED--

434
00:17:57,869 --> 00:18:00,371
THAT I'M JUST GOING
THROUGH A HARD TIME.

435
00:18:00,413 --> 00:18:01,497
WHAT'D HE SAY?

436
00:18:01,539 --> 00:18:03,123
WELL, UH, HIS ANSWERING MACHINE

437
00:18:03,165 --> 00:18:04,333
WAS VERY UNDERSTANDING.

438
00:18:06,794 --> 00:18:08,254
( sighs )

439
00:18:08,295 --> 00:18:10,339
I FEEL BLUE.

440
00:18:10,381 --> 00:18:12,842
AW, SWEETIE, OH...

441
00:18:12,884 --> 00:18:14,260
HONEY, I'LL BET
YOU ANYTHING

442
00:18:14,301 --> 00:18:15,929
HE'S GOING TO
CALL YOU AGAIN.

443
00:18:15,970 --> 00:18:20,725
YEAH, MAYBE, BUT, YOU KNOW,
I DON'T THINK I EVEN CARE.

444
00:18:20,767 --> 00:18:24,645
I DON'T THINK...
HE'S THE ONE I'M SAD ABOUT.

445
00:18:24,687 --> 00:18:26,606
YOU KNOW, I KNOW THAT I SAID

446
00:18:26,647 --> 00:18:29,483
I AM TOTALLY OKAY
WITH ROSS GETTING MARRIED

447
00:18:29,525 --> 00:18:31,151
BUT AS IT TURNS OUT

448
00:18:31,193 --> 00:18:34,113
I DON'T THINK I AM HANDLING IT
ALL THAT WELL.

449
00:18:34,154 --> 00:18:35,615
YEAH, MAYBE.

450
00:18:35,656 --> 00:18:39,786
AN-AND I'M JUST TRYING
TO FIGURE OUT WHY.

451
00:18:39,827 --> 00:18:40,995
ANY LUCK?

452
00:18:41,037 --> 00:18:42,872
YEAH, I MEAN, YOU KNOW,
HOW ROSS AND I

453
00:18:42,914 --> 00:18:44,874
HAVE ALWAYS BEEN
ON AGAIN, OFF AGAIN

454
00:18:44,916 --> 00:18:47,376
ON AGAIN, OFF AGAIN.

455
00:18:47,418 --> 00:18:51,129
I GUESS I JUST FIGURED
THAT SOMEWHERE DOWN THE ROAD...

456
00:18:51,171 --> 00:18:54,425
WE WOULD BE ON AGAIN... AGAIN.

457
00:18:54,467 --> 00:18:56,385
YOU KNOW WHAT?

458
00:18:56,427 --> 00:18:57,971
I THINK WE ALL DID.

459
00:18:58,012 --> 00:18:59,013
YEAH.

460
00:18:59,055 --> 00:19:00,431
HEY.

461
00:19:00,473 --> 00:19:01,474
HEY.
HEY.

462
00:19:06,479 --> 00:19:09,983
SO, GOT US RESERVATIONS
FOR SUNDAY NIGHT, OKAY?

463
00:19:10,024 --> 00:19:11,943
HOW ABOUT ERNIE'S AT 9:00?

464
00:19:11,985 --> 00:19:15,446
YEAH, WELL, YOU, UH,
BETTER MAKE IT FOR THREE.

465
00:19:15,488 --> 00:19:16,864
OH, SEE, I-I DON'T KNOW

466
00:19:16,906 --> 00:19:19,408
IF WE'RE GOING
TO BE HUNGRY AT 3:00.

467
00:19:21,159 --> 00:19:23,329
THREE PEOPLE.

468
00:19:23,370 --> 00:19:26,082
JOSHUA'S NOT GOING TO BE THERE.

469
00:19:26,124 --> 00:19:27,583
WHAT HAPPENED?

470
00:19:27,625 --> 00:19:30,003
UM, WELL, I THINK--
I THINK HE BROKE UP
WITH ME.

471
00:19:30,044 --> 00:19:32,212
NO. WHY?

472
00:19:32,254 --> 00:19:36,300
WELL... APPARENTLY,
HE SCARES EASY.

473
00:19:36,342 --> 00:19:38,886
OH, RACHEL, I'M SORRY.

474
00:19:38,928 --> 00:19:41,014
WELL... THAT'S OKAY.

475
00:19:41,055 --> 00:19:44,558
SOMETIMES... THINGS
DON'T WORK OUT

476
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:47,854
THE WAY YOU
THOUGHT THEY WOULD.

477
00:19:49,022 --> 00:19:49,981
COME HERE.

478
00:19:50,023 --> 00:19:51,231
OH...

479
00:19:51,273 --> 00:19:53,693
( sighs )

480
00:19:56,904 --> 00:19:58,614
WELL, HEY,
DON'T YOU HAVE

481
00:19:58,656 --> 00:20:00,158
TO GO PICK UP EMILY?

482
00:20:00,198 --> 00:20:01,325
YEAH.

483
00:20:01,367 --> 00:20:02,493
YEAH.

484
00:20:02,535 --> 00:20:03,703
ARE YOU OKAY?

485
00:20:03,744 --> 00:20:04,829
YEAH.

486
00:20:04,871 --> 00:20:06,288
I GOT MY GIRLS.

487
00:20:10,208 --> 00:20:11,335
OKAY.

488
00:20:16,049 --> 00:20:18,843
UGH.

489
00:20:18,885 --> 00:20:20,178
( groans )

490
00:20:20,219 --> 00:20:21,387
OH...

491
00:20:26,059 --> 00:20:29,353
HEY, YOU KNOW WHAT
MIGHT CHEER YOU UP?

492
00:20:29,395 --> 00:20:30,563
WHAT?

493
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:36,069
YOU KNOW,
I GOT TO TELL YOU

494
00:20:36,110 --> 00:20:38,696
THIS REALLY DOES PUT
ME IN A BETTER MOOD.

495
00:20:38,738 --> 00:20:40,156
MM-HMM.

496
00:20:40,198 --> 00:20:42,116
OH. I WISH THERE WAS A JOB

497
00:20:42,158 --> 00:20:45,369
WHERE I COULD WEAR THIS
ALL THE TIME.

498
00:20:45,411 --> 00:20:47,788
MAYBE SOMEDAY THERE WILL BE.

499
00:20:47,830 --> 00:20:49,331
( knock at door )

500
00:20:49,373 --> 00:20:50,791
OH, GOD, THAT'S CHANDLER.

501
00:20:50,833 --> 00:20:52,126
HE'S GOING TO COME BY

502
00:20:52,168 --> 00:20:54,294
AND BORROW SOME CANDLES
FOR HIS BIG DATE.

503
00:20:54,336 --> 00:20:55,546
OH, OKAY.

504
00:20:55,588 --> 00:20:57,255
RACHEL,
DON'T GET IT;
HE'LL SEE US.

505
00:20:57,297 --> 00:20:58,883
THE GROOM CANNOT
SEE THE BRIDE.

506
00:20:58,925 --> 00:21:00,968
YOU'RE NOT GOING
TO MARRY CHANDLER.

507
00:21:01,010 --> 00:21:03,303
NOT AFTER THIS.

508
00:21:04,513 --> 00:21:07,183
OKAY, GUYS... JUST RELAX.

509
00:21:12,188 --> 00:21:13,480
I DO...

510
00:21:17,484 --> 00:21:19,445
I GOT TO GO.

511
00:21:19,486 --> 00:21:20,821
OH, NO, JOSHUA...

512
00:21:20,863 --> 00:21:22,115
JOSHUA...

513
00:21:22,156 --> 00:21:23,365
OH...

514
00:21:24,867 --> 00:21:27,453
YEAH, WELL,
THAT OUGHT TO DO IT.

515
00:21:32,458 --> 00:21:33,626
FOOD'S HERE.

516
00:21:33,667 --> 00:21:35,211
FAIR ENOUGH.

517
00:21:35,253 --> 00:21:38,422
15-MINUTE WARNING!

518
00:21:38,464 --> 00:21:40,174
LATER...

519
00:21:44,470 --> 00:21:46,097
( shrieking )

520
00:21:46,139 --> 00:21:48,099
( screaming )

521
00:21:53,229 --> 00:21:59,152
( mumbling ):
DUDE, I AM TRYING TO SLEEP.

